{
  "_doc": [
    "Map storefront product slugs → threezerohk.com product-page URLs.",
    "The adapter fetches the page HTML, extracts JSON-LD Product data",
    "(or falls back to og: meta tags + a gallery sweep), and proposes",
    "description / sku / images.",
    "",
    "Two override shapes:",
    "  Existing product (slug already in `products` table):",
    "    \"figzero-naruto-uzumaki\": \"https://www.threezerohk.com/shop/3z0259-...\"",
    "",
    "  New product to be created as draft (slug NOT in `products`):",
    "    \"figzero-naruto-uzumaki\": {",
    "      \"url\": \"https://www.threezerohk.com/shop/3z0259-...\",",
    "      \"line\": \"figzero\",          /* required: product_lines slug */",
    "      \"name\": \"Naruto Uzumaki\"   /* optional: defaults to og:title */",
    "    }",
    "",
    "Before draft creation works you must:",
    "  1. Add brand `Three Zero` in /admin/settings?tab=brands",
    "  2. Add lines under it in /admin/settings?tab=lines, e.g.:",
    "       FigZero        (slug: figzero)",
    "       Robo-Dou       (slug: robo-dou)",
    "  3. Run: npm run crawl:apply -- --source=threezero",
    "",
    "_batches groups slugs so you can run a focused crawl:",
    "  npm run crawl:apply -- --source=threezero --batch=naruto",
    "",
    "_batch_series maps each batch to a default series name. When the",
    "runner creates a draft, it finds-or-creates a row in `series` and",
    "sets products.series_id."
  ],
